  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Program for complete educational trajectories and their climate resilience</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Programa de trayectorias educativas completas y su resiliencia al cambio climtico</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">El objetivo general del Programa es consolidar trayectorias educativas completas (acceso, aprendizaje y promocin) y su resiliencia al CC, los objetivos especficos son: (i) Incrementar la oferta educativa con resiliencia al CC focalizada en los niveles de parvularia y secundaria; (ii) Mejorar las prcticas directivas y pedaggicas para contribuir a la mejora de la calidad de los aprendizajes; (iii) incrementar el acceso a servicios educativos inclusivos para los EcD; (iv) incrementar la reinsercin educativa de personas migrantes retornadas; y (v) fortalecer las capacidades de gestin educativa, incluyendo las que integren medidas de mitigacin y adaptacin frente al CC (desarrollo de una cartera de proyectos, y monitoreo y reporte de impacto), contribuyendo a fortalecer las condiciones del pas de acceso a financiamiento climtico.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The general objective of the Program is to consolidate complete educational trajectories (access, learning, and promotion) and their resilience to climate change (CC). The specific objectives are: (i) to increase the supply of climate-resilient educational services, focusing on early childhood and secondary education levels; (ii) to improve school leadership and pedagogical practices to enhance the quality of learning outcomes; (iii) to expand access to inclusive educational services for children with disabilities (SwD); (iv) to increase the educational reintegration of returned migrant populations; and (v) to strengthen education management capacities, including those that incorporate mitigation and adaptation measures to address CC (such as the development of a project portfolio, and monitoring and impact reporting), thereby contributing to enhancing the country&apos;s conditions for access to climate financing.</narrative>
  </description>
